1
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:12,267
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:41,233
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:43,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,833
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,567 --> 00:00:56,967
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:00,867
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,333
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:04,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,600
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,900
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,600
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:19,567
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,367
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:23,067 --> 00:01:25,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:28,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:36,267
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,967 --> 00:01:39,267
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:48,800
<i> That's Ma'am Pia's report.</i>

24
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:51,833
<i>Mandatory leadership and
operational compliance training.</i>

25
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:53,100
<i> Possible suspension.</i>

26
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:56,433
<i>If that man wasn't involved
in your operation</i>

27
00:01:56,567 --> 00:01:59,067
<i> the report would be different.</i>

28
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,833
<i>Where did you take
the motorcycle?</i>

29
00:02:00,967 --> 00:02:03,300
<i>There was a mishap
so I had to leave it.</i>

30
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:06,833
<i>The money he'll pay is
for your dad's medical expenses!</i>

31
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:08,267
<i> You failed!</i>

32
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,500
<i> Now the money's gone!</i>

33
00:02:10,633 --> 00:02:12,500
<i> Don't worry. I'll get it back.</i>

34
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:14,200
<i>We can't just walk in
through there.</i>

35
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:15,600
<i> We'll go through the back.</i>

36
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:17,733
<i>The man who messed up
our operation.</i>

37
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:19,500
<i> I believe that guy is the key</i>

38
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,633
<i>for us to solve
this gold smuggling case.</i>

39
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:23,933
<i>Get every piece of information
linked to that motorcycle.</i>

40
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:26,733
<i>It will lead the way
for me to find him.</i>

41
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:28,133
<i>I need to get
the motorcycle back.</i>

42
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:30,100
Look carefully. Let's split up.

43
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:33,267
[ARNEL] Miss KC,

44
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,433
what was it [SIGHS]

45
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:37,567
that you want to talk about?

46
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:39,200
It's about Salvador.

47
00:02:39,433 --> 00:02:40,600
Miss KC,

48
00:02:40,733 --> 00:02:42,633
I did everything I could.

49
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:44,867
I squeezed him dry

50
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,933
just to improve his reports!

51
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,167
It did improve!

52
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:49,933
The ratings increased.

53
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:51,333
The public is very invested.

54
00:02:51,467 --> 00:02:54,800
Salvador's report is a hit!

55
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:56,433
You're welcome, Ma'am!

56
00:02:56,567 --> 00:02:58,867
It was me who really brought out
the best in Salvador!

57
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,867
I'll have you know,
it was thanks to me, ma'am!

58
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,033
We will capitalize
on this, Arnel.

59
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:05,600
- It's time
- Yes, ma'am.

60
00:03:05,733 --> 00:03:07,567
for us to really sell Salvador
out here.

61
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:11,133
- Yes, ma'am.
- We'll give Salvador a show

62
00:03:11,267 --> 00:03:14,400
where he will be
the host himself.

63
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:16,967
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,233
Oli.

65
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:21,033
I went home
while the commander's mad.

66
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,767
[CLATTERING]

67
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,567
- [SIGHS]
- [DOOR OPENS]

68
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,967
Salvador! Salvador!
[PANTING]

69
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,967
Get rid of those
reporter clothes!

70
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,533
You are going to be a host!

71
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:34,200
Hose? Like a garden hose?

72
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:35,600
No, Salvador!

73
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:40,233
- You will have your own show!
- Show...

74
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:42,267
And you are the star!

75
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:45,300
Even if you don't look like one!

76
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:46,733
Even if you don't
look like a star,

77
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:51,000
your name will be known
by the entire country

78
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:54,933
as Salvador Manalo.

79
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:58,867
Congratulations!
Congratulations, you're amazing!

80
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,667
[STUTTERING] Congratulations!
You did so well!

81
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:04,267
- Boss, hold on.
- Yeah?

82
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:06,433
Boss, get this.

83
00:04:07,167 --> 00:04:08,733
Once I strike it big,

84
00:04:08,867 --> 00:04:10,600
I promise you,

85
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:12,533
I won't forget about you.

86
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:16,767
You know what, we just need
to do a makeover.

87
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,233
N-- not too much makeover,
I hope.

88
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:22,133
Don't stray too far
from how people knew me

89
00:04:22,267 --> 00:04:23,933
they might just get confused.

90
00:04:24,067 --> 00:04:25,267
Did you become popular?

91
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,467
You didn't, right?

92
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:31,233
That's why we'll change it
and give you a cooler image!

93
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,300
I mean, you do look brave

94
00:04:33,433 --> 00:04:35,733
despite your short height
and dark skin.

95
00:04:35,867 --> 00:04:37,033
But don't worry.

96
00:04:37,167 --> 00:04:40,033
We'll gradually change you,
starting from the way you dress.

97
00:04:40,167 --> 00:04:41,667
You made the most of it,
didn't you, boss?

98
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,833
You mixed insults
with your compliments.

99
00:04:43,967 --> 00:04:49,967
You just have to look like
the enemy of wicked men!

100
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,600
You'll fight
against all the criminals!

101
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:56,200
All of them
will be scared of you!

102
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,500
What if this kills me?

103
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:00,933
That is part of the job.

104
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:04,333
[DOOR OPENS, SHUTS]

105
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,600
I'm just trying
to understand her.

106
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:09,000
Her mind's still clouded.

107
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:11,500
[RALLOS] Sir, now is when
she needs you most.

108
00:05:11,633 --> 00:05:13,400
You have to make an effort now.

109
00:05:13,533 --> 00:05:14,733
Timing is everything.

110
00:05:15,333 --> 00:05:18,000
The only thing
I can tell you now, Sir Seb...

111
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,133
...is don't lose hope

112
00:05:20,267 --> 00:05:23,600
because to me,
you are still the one.

113
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,833
I won't approach her for now,
while her mind's still clouded.

114
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:29,967
[RALLOS] But, sir,
you can make an effort

115
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,933
without annoying her.

116
00:05:33,567 --> 00:05:34,900
What do you mean?

117
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:38,200
- Have you spoken to Ma'am Pia?
- That's right, sir.

118
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:42,033
Ma'am Pia might change
her assessment of our case.

119
00:05:42,167 --> 00:05:44,900
[RALLOS] And if you do that
great favor for Ma'am Sam,

120
00:05:45,033 --> 00:05:48,167
she'll appreciate you even more!
You'll be the star, sir.

121
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,133
[KAREN] And she'll fall in love
with you

122
00:05:50,267 --> 00:05:52,467
because you are the answer
to her problems.

123
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:57,367
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

124
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,467
[HANDS CLAP]

125
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,667
[PAPERS RUSTLE]

126
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,667
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

127
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,733
Ma'am Pia.

128
00:06:05,167 --> 00:06:06,133
[PIA CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

129
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,367
Ma'am Pia?

130
00:06:08,467 --> 00:06:08,867
[PIA CLEARS THROAT]

131
00:06:09,367 --> 00:06:11,867
Call me Pia.
It's just us here, anyway.

132
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:12,733
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

133
00:06:13,233 --> 00:06:15,700
I'd rather call you Ma'am Pia.

134
00:06:17,567 --> 00:06:19,600
So, ma'am, uh...

135
00:06:19,733 --> 00:06:22,067
Regarding your assessment
of Sam.

136
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:25,033
I believe your assessment
of her performance

137
00:06:25,167 --> 00:06:26,500
was inaccurate.

138
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,200
Why are you...

139
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,267
...so concerned about her?

140
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:38,833
[DOOR SLIDING]

141
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,100
Didn't you like...

142
00:06:49,733 --> 00:06:53,033
...the good review
I gave you?

143
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:54,800
No, no, no, ma'am.

144
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:58,433
I am truly grateful,
and I thank you.

145
00:07:00,767 --> 00:07:02,000
And you're grateful.

146
00:07:03,367 --> 00:07:04,333
Mm-hmm.

147
00:07:04,967 --> 00:07:06,867
Hmm...

148
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,300
You know, Sebastian...

149
00:07:09,467 --> 00:07:11,333
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:07:11,467 --> 00:07:14,333
You won't gain anything
from Jacinto.

151
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,733
The top of the NCIA ladder...

152
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:21,400
...is too high.

153
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:23,867
You should be smart
in choosing your connections,

154
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,833
so you can climb
that ladder quickly.

155
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:26,833
[SEBASTIAN SCOFFS]

156
00:07:26,967 --> 00:07:29,333
You know, ma'am,
I didn't really dream of--

157
00:07:29,467 --> 00:07:30,667
Shh!

158
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:33,433
[PIA TUTTING]

159
00:07:33,567 --> 00:07:34,533
Shh...

160
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:39,167
Everyone wants to reach
the top.

161
00:07:39,733 --> 00:07:41,000
I'm already on top.

162
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:45,367
Believe me, Sebastian.

163
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:47,867
It's great up here.

164
00:07:49,667 --> 00:07:51,967
It's very, very great.

165
00:07:53,367 --> 00:07:57,400
I can do a lot of things
for you.

166
00:07:57,533 --> 00:07:59,000
[PIA INHALES SHARPLY]

167
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,567
Just say the word.

168
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:09,667
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,400
[DOOR SLIDING]

170
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:34,233
[STEALTHY MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:08:35,933 --> 00:08:38,033
Tolits, there are
so many cars here.

172
00:08:38,167 --> 00:08:39,433
Some are even rotting!

173
00:08:40,267 --> 00:08:42,433
Seems like you fit in here.
You're rotting too.

174
00:08:42,567 --> 00:08:44,433
- Huh? Why me?
- Shush!

175
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:46,533
You're too noisy,
don't be noisy!

176
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:53,333
The next time we go here,
we'll rob a nice car,

177
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:55,567
so we look handsome
when we go out!

178
00:08:55,733 --> 00:08:57,533
[DABOY] I'd love to have
a Beetle.

179
00:08:57,667 --> 00:08:59,767
- That car suits me just fine!
- A Beetle?

180
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,033
How will you even fit there
with that belly?

181
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,567
- Shush, shush, shush!
- Hold me back!

182
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:07,133
- Don't be loud!
- You're loud!

183
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:08,467
- There's someone!
- Hey!

184
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,433
[BINOY] There's someone!
Let's hide here, c'mon!

185
00:09:13,733 --> 00:09:17,600
[STEALTHY MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:18,967
[TEKLA] Gabo!

187
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,267
Why did you have to mess

188
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,333
with the motorbike
Sir Rudy's fixing?

189
00:09:22,467 --> 00:09:24,100
Now you're in a mess!

190
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:25,300
[GABO SIGHS]

191
00:09:25,433 --> 00:09:27,767
I didn't know. I just want him
to get his surgery.

192
00:09:28,467 --> 00:09:29,600
That's why I took it.

193
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:33,200
I get it,
but now it's a mess!

194
00:09:33,767 --> 00:09:36,667
What are we going to do now?
Miss Betchay is so mad at you.

195
00:09:37,467 --> 00:09:38,867
Mama Betchay's
always been like that.

196
00:09:39,667 --> 00:09:40,700
Even when I was a kid...

197
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,500
She was often mad at me.

198
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:49,567
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:09:51,033 --> 00:09:52,900
- Do you see those guys?
- [EXHALES]

200
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,867
Tekla.

201
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:57,800
Use your beauty and charm.

202
00:09:59,467 --> 00:10:02,567
Act like you have questions
for them.

203
00:10:03,133 --> 00:10:05,033
Find out where the
motor parts are located,

204
00:10:05,167 --> 00:10:09,533
then ask where they store
the motorcycles.

205
00:10:09,667 --> 00:10:10,667
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,800
I'm your girl.

207
00:10:11,933 --> 00:10:13,500
You can count on me, Gabo.

208
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:15,600
I'll play my beauty
and charm card.

209
00:10:16,467 --> 00:10:18,400
- Okay.
- I've got this.

210
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:21,133
Be careful.

211
00:10:25,267 --> 00:10:32,233
[QUIRKY TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,600
- [BONG] Someone's coming!
- [DABOY] Hurry!

213
00:10:35,733 --> 00:10:36,867
- Come on!
- Over there!

214
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,967
- Down here!
- Move it!

215
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:39,367
- Get down!
- [BINOY] Ouch!

216
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:40,800
Shush!

217
00:10:41,867 --> 00:10:43,133
[TOLITS WHISPERS]
Don't make a sound!

218
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:45,200
[THUDS]

219
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:53,867
- [PEE TRICKLING]
- [QUIRKY TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:10:57,367 --> 00:10:58,300
[ZIPPER RASPS]

221
00:10:59,133 --> 00:11:00,267
Come on, keep going!

222
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,400
Boys, follow me!

223
00:11:01,533 --> 00:11:02,567
- Help me!
- [GROANS]

224
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,767
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

225
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:04,967
[TOLITS, BINOY GRUNT]

226
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,067
Come on!

227
00:11:08,233 --> 00:11:09,933
[FLIRTY MUSIC PLAYING]

228
00:11:10,067 --> 00:11:11,100
[MAN 1] Hey, guys.

229
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:13,633
The motorcycle delivered
last night was stunning.

230
00:11:13,767 --> 00:11:15,300
Do you think they'll pick it up?

231
00:11:15,433 --> 00:11:16,967
- [MAN 2] Not a chance.
- [MAN 3] Probably not.

232
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:19,200
[MAN 1] I hope not, so we can
dismantle it for parts.

233
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,533
[MAN 4] Bro, that woman is hot.

234
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:25,800
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

235
00:11:25,933 --> 00:11:26,967
- Hey, boys.
- [MAN 2] Miss...

236
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,200
How can we help you?

237
00:11:28,333 --> 00:11:33,533
[FLIRTY MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:11:33,667 --> 00:11:37,600
I was hoping to ask
if you sell parts here.

239
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:39,967
[MAN 1] Miss, what kind
of parts are you looking for?

240
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,300
For motorcycles,
if you have them here.

241
00:11:42,467 --> 00:11:44,067
- Plenty, in fact.
- My big bike crashed.

242
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,333
When I brought it
to the repair shop,

243
00:11:45,467 --> 00:11:48,000
the charge was pretty expensive.

244
00:11:48,133 --> 00:11:49,667
Maybe you've got the parts here.

245
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,000
[MAN 2]
We definitely have them here.

246
00:11:51,133 --> 00:11:52,533
They might be pricey, though.

247
00:11:52,667 --> 00:11:54,200
Please don't charge
me too much.

248
00:11:54,333 --> 00:11:56,000
[MAN 3] Well, that depends.
We can talk about it.

249
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:57,000
[GIGGLES]

250
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,100
[MAN 1] Miss...

251
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,233
Are you with someone?

252
00:12:00,367 --> 00:12:02,433
Oh. Why?

253
00:12:02,567 --> 00:12:04,633
Do you see someone
I don't, mister?

254
00:12:04,767 --> 00:12:06,500
No! I came here on my own.

255
00:12:06,633 --> 00:12:07,867
I worked up the courage,

256
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,333
hoping maybe you've got
cheaper parts.

257
00:12:10,467 --> 00:12:12,133
Good thing you do.

258
00:12:12,267 --> 00:12:13,100
Where are they?

259
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:14,767
Let's discuss it in our office.

260
00:12:14,933 --> 00:12:16,933
Sure thing.
Where's your office?

261
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:18,800
- [MAN 3] Come on, join us.
- This way?

262
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:29,300
[MUSIC BECOMES THRILLING]

263
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:44,833
[SIGHS]

264
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:47,533
[TEASPON CLINKING]

265
00:12:47,533 --> 00:12:48,633
[CHAIR RATTLES]

266
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:50,800
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

267
00:12:53,133 --> 00:12:54,133
[ERNESTO CLEARS THROAT]

268
00:12:54,667 --> 00:12:56,433
Sir, have you talked
to Ma'am Pia?

269
00:12:56,433 --> 00:12:57,500
Mm-hmm.

270
00:12:57,933 --> 00:12:58,933
I tried.

271
00:12:58,933 --> 00:13:01,633
So, sir, why do you seem
more troubled?

272
00:13:01,633 --> 00:13:02,733
[SEBASTIAN] I could tell...

273
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:04,967
she didn't want to talk
about Sam.

274
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,667
Bad timing, maybe.

275
00:13:09,633 --> 00:13:12,233
But I'll take it slow with her.

276
00:13:12,233 --> 00:13:13,400
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,400
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

278
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:15,567
For Sam.

279
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:25,867
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,833
[BOSS]
All you do is talk endlessly!

281
00:13:27,833 --> 00:13:29,533
- Hide now!
- They're heading this way!

282
00:13:30,567 --> 00:13:31,667
Hurry up!

283
00:13:31,667 --> 00:13:32,700
[BOSS] You keep wasting time!

284
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,500
Why is that car door open?

285
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:35,633
I've warned you before!

286
00:13:35,633 --> 00:13:36,667
[CAR DOOR SLAMS SHUT]

287
00:13:36,667 --> 00:13:37,733
Argh...

288
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,433
Shush, shush! Get out!

289
00:13:41,633 --> 00:13:42,900
Come on, let's go!

290
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:45,167
[WORKER 1] Perfect timing.
There's a brand-new motorcycle.

291
00:13:45,167 --> 00:13:46,600
- Really?
- Yes!

292
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,233
- What color?
- Miss, it's black!

293
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:52,200
And guess what?
It was delivered last night!

294
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,100
- It's stunning!
- Oh! That sounds like heaven!

295
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,900
- My motorcycle is also black!
- Then it's a match!

296
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:58,433
Could you show it to me?
Lead the way, please!

297
00:13:58,433 --> 00:14:00,733
We'll give it to you for free.

298
00:14:00,733 --> 00:14:03,433
Oh, that's too much!
Is it really free?

299
00:14:03,433 --> 00:14:04,533
- Absolutely!
- Yeah!

300
00:14:04,533 --> 00:14:06,900
So you won't have to spend
too much! Right, boys?

301
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,900
Hey, wait a minute! Hang on!

302
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,667
What if I can't give
what you want in return?

303
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:14,100
- Of course you can!
- You can do it!

304
00:14:15,567 --> 00:14:22,633
[EXCITING MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:14:22,933 --> 00:14:25,867
[THUDDING]

306
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:31,833
[THUDDING]

307
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:36,100
[WORKER 2] We'll go over
the details in the office.

308
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:37,233
- Right, boys?
- Yeah, right!

309
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:38,200
[TEKLA] Okay, where is it?

310
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:42,200
[EXCITING MUSIC CONTINUES]

311
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,367
[TEKLA] Don't scam me, okay?

312
00:14:43,367 --> 00:14:47,667
[THUDDING]

313
00:14:47,667 --> 00:14:48,767
[CAR DOOR RATTLES]

314
00:14:48,767 --> 00:14:50,633
[TEKLA] Feels like you're
trying to rip me off!

315
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:52,067
[METAL PARTS CLANK]

316
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:53,567
[AIR WHOOSHING]

317
00:14:53,567 --> 00:14:54,600
[SOFT THUD]

318
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:01,633
[TEKLA] Wow, I got lucky
meeting you boys today.

319
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:04,633
Now, I won't have to spend big
to get my motorcycle fixed.

320
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:07,133
[WORKER 3] You won't have
to spend a thing!

321
00:15:07,133 --> 00:15:08,933
Because we're giving it to you!

322
00:15:08,933 --> 00:15:10,667
[TEKLA GASPS] Seriously?!

323
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:13,100
- That's right!
- Just be a good girl...

324
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:15,333
and we'll give you
whatever you want.

325
00:15:15,333 --> 00:15:16,433
[TEKLA] Oh, alright then!

326
00:15:16,433 --> 00:15:17,767
So where's the motorcycle?

327
00:15:17,767 --> 00:15:19,700
Where is it? That one?

328
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:22,167
B-But it's all busted up!

329
00:15:22,833 --> 00:15:24,033
[WORKER 2] Not that one, miss.

330
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:25,667
That one!

331
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,933
- Where?
- Over there! Come on!

332
00:15:27,933 --> 00:15:29,167
- That one?
- Yeah!

333
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:30,267
Take a look!

334
00:15:30,267 --> 00:15:31,467
- Stunning, right?
- Wow!

335
00:15:31,467 --> 00:15:33,433
- What a motorcycle!
- It's yours now!

336
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:36,033
- So handsome!
- Right?

337
00:15:36,067 --> 00:15:37,900
- Look!
- It's stunning!

338
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,433
- It really is!
- Yeah!

339
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:42,633
If you want, you can have it.

340
00:15:43,633 --> 00:15:45,267
- Exactly!
- Are you sure?

341
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:46,533
Here's the key.

342
00:15:46,533 --> 00:15:47,533
- [HIGH FIVE]
- [GIGGLES]

343
00:15:47,533 --> 00:15:49,367
- Can I fire it up?
- Of course!

344
00:15:49,367 --> 00:15:50,900
- Go on!
- Oh my!

345
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,533
- Perfect!
- [HANDS CLAP]

346
00:15:52,533 --> 00:15:53,700
[EXCITING MUSIC CONTINUES]

347
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,067
[KEY TURNS]

348
00:15:55,067 --> 00:15:56,167
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

349
00:15:56,167 --> 00:15:57,633
[ENGINE STARTS]

350
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:59,667
- Oh my!
- [WORKER 2] Hear that?

351
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,967
[TEKLA] It's just perfect! Wow!

352
00:16:01,967 --> 00:16:04,400
It's better than my old bike!
The sound is awesome!

353
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,967
- It suits me, right?
- Absolutely!

354
00:16:05,967 --> 00:16:09,033
We'll give you everything
you want here.

355
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,133
Just make sure...

356
00:16:11,533 --> 00:16:13,467
you give us what we want
from you.

357
00:16:13,467 --> 00:16:14,467
- Right, boys?
- Oh, yes!

358
00:16:14,467 --> 00:16:16,233
- Well, of course!
- There we go!

359
00:16:16,233 --> 00:16:18,400
So it's settled.
This is mine now.

360
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,833
[WORKER 2] Come on, miss.

361
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:21,333
Join us at the office.

362
00:16:21,333 --> 00:16:23,333
We'll fix the release papers

363
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:24,900
so you can bring
your motorcycle home!

364
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:25,900
- Right, boys?
- Totally!

365
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,800
Wow, you're all so kind!

366
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,033
- Come on, let's go!
- This way, miss!

367
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:32,867
- Hurry up, boys!
- Follow us!

368
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:33,933
It's just over here!

369
00:16:33,933 --> 00:16:40,833
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:16:55,633 --> 00:17:02,433
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:17:02,433 --> 00:17:03,500
[KEY TURNS]

372
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,567
[ENGINE RUMBLING]

373
00:17:04,567 --> 00:17:07,067
[ENGINE ROARING, REVVING]

374
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:12,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

375
00:17:12,233 --> 00:17:13,700
Are we sure
the motorcycle is here?

376
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:14,900
Maybe we're just looking
for nothing.

377
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:16,533
We're just going around
in circles.

378
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:17,733
I'm so tired.

379
00:17:17,733 --> 00:17:19,433
Tolits, I'm hungry.

380
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:21,433
Talking won't help us find it.

381
00:17:21,433 --> 00:17:22,700
It's here somewhere.

382
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,667
If it's really here,
then where is it?

383
00:17:26,633 --> 00:17:33,600
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:17:35,567 --> 00:17:37,733
[ENGINE REVVING]

385
00:17:38,267 --> 00:17:40,933
Where the hell is your office?
We've been walking forever.

386
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:42,800
Are you guys screwing with me?

387
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,233
Miss, the office
is just up ahead.

388
00:17:45,233 --> 00:17:46,767
- Right here?
- So we can fix

389
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:48,233
your motorcycle's
release papers.

390
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:49,933
- Yeah.
- Okay?

391
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:52,500
You better keep
your word, guys.

392
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,467
- Of course, it's just--
- Get it transferred to my name.

393
00:17:54,467 --> 00:17:56,867
- This way.
- Here?

394
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:59,100
The office is right around
the back, miss.

395
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:00,333
- In the back?!
- Yes!

396
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:02,500
An office back there?
Is that even allowed?

397
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,900
That's where we always
process the papers.

398
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,700
- Alright, fine.
- It's much faster.

399
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,800
It's just right around here.

400
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:11,433
Just make sure my bike
gets released fast, okay?

401
00:18:11,433 --> 00:18:12,867
Look, a dog!
[MAKING PSSTING SOUNDS]

402
00:18:12,867 --> 00:18:15,600
Look how cute it is.
[GIGGLES]

403
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,767
It definitely got impounded,
since it's here.

404
00:18:17,767 --> 00:18:20,400
Maybe its registration expired.

405
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,500
Registration?

406
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:25,300
Registration? It's a dog,
its owner just left it.

407
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:26,600
[DOGS GROWLING]

408
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:31,367
Once we find the bike,
we're taking this dog home.

409
00:18:31,367 --> 00:18:37,133
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [DOGS BARKING]

410
00:18:37,133 --> 00:18:39,667
- [DOGS SNARLING]
- Oh...

411
00:18:39,667 --> 00:18:42,400
- [MOUTHING WORDS] One, two...
- Don't move.

412
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:46,500
If we move,
they'll maul us.

413
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:49,267
My grandpa said never run
from a dog.

414
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:54,467
Try smiling
so they get good vibes.

415
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,700
No?

416
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,467
[DOGS GROWLING, BARKING]

417
00:18:57,467 --> 00:18:59,000
[WHIMPERS]

418
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,433
Don't worry, I know dogs,
I'm an animal lover.

419
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:04,000
- Go on then, try it.
- Okay.

420
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,967
- Just stay quiet.
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:19:05,967 --> 00:19:07,033
[MAKING PSSTING SOUNDS]

422
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:09,633
- You're calling them wrong!
- [BINOY WHIMPERS]

423
00:19:09,633 --> 00:19:11,167
You're making cat sounds.

424
00:19:11,167 --> 00:19:13,933
They're dogs,
so use dog language.

425
00:19:13,933 --> 00:19:16,200
- You know dog language?
- A little bit.

426
00:19:18,467 --> 00:19:22,733
[MIMICS GROWLING]

427
00:19:25,233 --> 00:19:27,733
- [MIMICS GROWLING] Argh!
- [DOG BARKS]

428
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,167
What the hell are you doing?!
What on earth are you saying?!

429
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:34,433
Let me try, let me work
my charm on them.

430
00:19:34,433 --> 00:19:36,367
[DOGS GROWLING]

431
00:19:36,367 --> 00:19:38,433
Sit down.

432
00:19:38,433 --> 00:19:39,733
[GROWLS]

433
00:19:39,733 --> 00:19:42,567
- [SHRIEKS]
- Hey! Don't ever do that again!

434
00:19:42,567 --> 00:19:45,033
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

435
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:48,967
- [KEYS JINGLE]
- [ENGINE TURNS OFF]

436
00:19:48,967 --> 00:19:55,367
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING,
THEN FADES]

437
00:19:55,367 --> 00:19:57,033
- Right here, miss.
- Here?

438
00:19:57,033 --> 00:19:58,067
- Hey, man.
- Yeah?

439
00:19:58,067 --> 00:20:00,367
- What is this place? It's...
- What's up?

440
00:20:00,367 --> 00:20:01,867
Hey, this looks
like a barracks--

441
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:04,300
She's looking for
motorcycle parts.

442
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,467
What are you going
to do to me?

443
00:20:05,467 --> 00:20:08,367
We were going to give her
the bike that just came in.

444
00:20:08,367 --> 00:20:09,567
Oh, is that so?

445
00:20:09,567 --> 00:20:13,433
We'll clear her papers
so she can get it, man.

446
00:20:13,433 --> 00:20:16,133
[MAN] Alright, bring her in.

447
00:20:16,133 --> 00:20:18,000
Can't we just stay out here?

448
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,100
Hey, wait!
What are you doing?!

449
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:21,400
- Get inside!
- Get off me!

450
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,700
- I said get in!
- [SCREAMS] What are you doing?!

451
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:25,700
- Get in there!
- [GRUNTS LOUDLY]

452
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:27,900
Look where that got you!
[LAUGHS]

453
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:30,567
- You bastards! [KICK LANDS]
- [GRUNTS IN PAIN]

454
00:20:30,567 --> 00:20:32,700
[SMACKS, KICK LANDS]

455
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,367
- [SCREAMING]
- [GRUNTING]

456
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:36,333
- Sit down!
- [BODY THUDS]

457
00:20:36,367 --> 00:20:43,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

458
00:20:45,067 --> 00:20:51,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

459
00:21:03,067 --> 00:21:04,067
[BARKING]

460
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,233
- Run!
- Run!

461
00:21:05,367 --> 00:21:12,133
- [DOGS BARKING]
- [CLAMORING]

462
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:19,167
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

463
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:23,500
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

464
00:21:23,633 --> 00:21:24,667
Hey, who are you?

465
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:28,267
Uh, sir, I'm just looking
for my female companion.

466
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,200
She's wearing a red top
and pink shorts.

467
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:32,267
There's no woman here
with that description.

468
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:34,367
<i>- You think you can run?!
- Just you try!</i>

469
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,367
- [TEKLA SCREAMS] Help!
- Hold her down!

470
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,067
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

471
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,167
[BLOWS LANDING]

472
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:42,933
[TEKLA] Let me go!

473
00:21:43,067 --> 00:21:47,300
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [YELLING]

474
00:21:48,267 --> 00:21:49,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Hey!

475
00:21:50,033 --> 00:21:54,500
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTS, GROANING]

476
00:21:54,633 --> 00:21:56,233
[ECHOING BLOW]

477
00:21:57,767 --> 00:21:58,800
[THWACKS]

478
00:21:58,933 --> 00:22:02,200
[BLOWS LANDING]

479
00:22:02,333 --> 00:22:03,300
[SLAMS]

480
00:22:03,433 --> 00:22:05,733
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [BODY SLAMMING]

481
00:22:05,867 --> 00:22:09,900
[DOGS BARKING]

482
00:22:10,033 --> 00:22:15,000
[BLOWS LANDING]

483
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:17,033
[DOGS BARKING]

484
00:22:17,167 --> 00:22:19,233
- Gabo!
- Tekla! Let's go!

485
00:22:19,367 --> 00:22:20,533
[MEN GROANING]

486
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:22,333
Hey! Catch them!

487
00:22:22,467 --> 00:22:23,933
Everyone, this way!

488
00:22:24,067 --> 00:22:25,467
- Hurry!
- Come on!

489
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,333
[PANICKED SCREAMING]

490
00:22:27,467 --> 00:22:30,267
Come closer, and I'll bite you!
You want that, huh?!

491
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,433
Catch them!

492
00:22:32,867 --> 00:22:34,933
- Move!
- Out of the way!

493
00:22:35,067 --> 00:22:36,233
Move!

494
00:22:36,367 --> 00:22:39,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

495
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,633
Run! I'll distract them!

496
00:22:41,767 --> 00:22:42,833
They're coming!

497
00:22:42,967 --> 00:22:44,067
[TEKLA PANTING]

498
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:51,067
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

499
00:22:51,233 --> 00:22:56,567
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

500
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:58,067
He went that way! Hurry!

501
00:22:59,567 --> 00:23:01,433
[MUD SQUELCHING]

502
00:23:01,567 --> 00:23:02,467
[BRAKES SCREECH]

503
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,000
- Leave us alone!
- [DOGS BARKING]

504
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:05,900
Gabo! It's Gabo!

505
00:23:06,033 --> 00:23:07,200
Gabo!

506
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:08,567
[WHISTLES]

507
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:10,700
[BARKING STOPS]

508
00:23:10,833 --> 00:23:17,900
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [DOGS BARKING]

509
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,500
Come on! Let's go!

510
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:29,467
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

511
00:23:38,633 --> 00:23:41,233
[PANTING]

512
00:23:41,367 --> 00:23:42,533
Hurry! Come on!

513
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:44,900
- Faster!
- It's Tekla!

514
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:47,600
- Tekla!
- Let's bounce!

515
00:23:47,733 --> 00:23:49,867
- Gabo's got his bike!
- Good! Let's scram!

516
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:53,600
- Which way's the exit?!
- This way!

517
00:23:54,633 --> 00:24:01,500
- [DOGS BARKING]
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

518
00:24:05,567 --> 00:24:09,333
[SCREAMING]

519
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:14,133
[LOUD CRASH]

520
00:24:15,967 --> 00:24:16,967
- Come on!
- Let's go!

521
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:18,233
- Run! Hurry!
- Move! Move!

522
00:24:19,067 --> 00:24:20,600
Go! Go! Go!

523
00:24:20,733 --> 00:24:23,333
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARS]
- [DOGS BARKING]

524
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:26,633
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]
- [THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

525
00:24:27,667 --> 00:24:29,200
- Come on!
- Hurry!

526
00:24:31,733 --> 00:24:33,067
- Faster!
- Move!

527
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:34,400
Run!

528
00:24:40,167 --> 00:24:41,467
- [COUGHING]
- You good?

529
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:42,700
They didn't catch you?

530
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:45,167
Good thing we got away!

531
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:47,000
We were almost eaten by dogs!

532
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:48,300
That all?!

533
00:24:48,433 --> 00:24:51,267
I almost got raped!
Good thing Gabo saved me.

534
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,333
- Huh?
- What?

535
00:24:53,233 --> 00:24:55,767
I'm sorry you got
dragged into this.

536
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:58,167
But thank you so much
for your help.

537
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:00,333
Thanks to you,
I got this bike back.

538
00:25:00,467 --> 00:25:01,833
Don't mention it, Gabo.

539
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,233
We promised we'd do everything

540
00:25:04,367 --> 00:25:07,167
to help with
Mister Rudy's treatment.

541
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:11,867
We should go. I'll meet you
later at Ginintuang Lupa.

542
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:15,400
I'll drop by the hospital first
to check on Papa.

543
00:25:15,533 --> 00:25:17,267
Alright. Take care, Gabo.
See you later.

544
00:25:18,067 --> 00:25:19,300
You be careful too.

545
00:25:19,433 --> 00:25:21,333
You better go
before they find you.

546
00:25:21,467 --> 00:25:24,467
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

547
00:25:25,533 --> 00:25:27,100
<i> I have a mission for you.</i>

548
00:25:28,133 --> 00:25:31,833
<i> Mr. Chan took the gold bars.</i>

549
00:25:31,967 --> 00:25:35,033
<i>He'll be our key to proving
that Tiger is guilty.</i>

550
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,333
<i>I can't control
my daughter, Samantha.</i>

551
00:25:37,467 --> 00:25:38,667
<i> You were a general.</i>

552
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:42,100
<i>Now, you can't even control
your low-ranked daughter?!</i>

553
00:25:42,233 --> 00:25:47,633
<i>I'm sure they'll use Mr. Chan
to testify against Victor.</i>

554
00:25:47,767 --> 00:25:50,567
<i>We have to make sure
he doesn't squeak.</i>

555
00:25:51,833 --> 00:25:53,000
[GUNSHOTS]

556
00:25:53,133 --> 00:25:56,533
<i>We need to get ahead
of our enemies.</i>

557
00:25:56,667 --> 00:26:00,800
<i>You need to take the gold bars
from Mr. Chan.</i>

558
00:26:00,933 --> 00:26:02,933
<i>I don't care if he dies
or not.</i>

559
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:06,000
[GUNSHOTS]

560
00:26:06,133 --> 00:26:07,300
<i>- Let's go!
- Get inside!</i>

561
00:26:07,433 --> 00:26:09,733
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

562
00:26:10,333 --> 00:26:11,367
- [GUNSHOTS]
<i> - Surround them!</i>

563
00:26:11,500 --> 00:26:13,067
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

564
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:15,333
<i>Umali will pay us
a huge sum.</i>

565
00:26:15,467 --> 00:26:18,167
<i> I want you to do the job.</i>

566
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:19,467
<i> I'll take care of it.</i>

567
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:21,667
- [THWACKS]
- [SCREAMS]

568
00:26:22,733 --> 00:26:24,000
- [GUNSHOTS]
<i> - Mr. Chan!</i>

569
00:26:24,133 --> 00:26:26,067
[BLOWS LANDING]

570
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:27,767
- [LOUD CRASH]
- What's your name?

571
00:26:28,533 --> 00:26:29,500
<i> Gabo.</i>

572
00:26:29,933 --> 00:26:33,367
<i>Your father doesn't have
much time left.</i>

573
00:26:34,100 --> 00:26:35,800
<i> Doc! Help! Help!</i>

574
00:26:35,933 --> 00:26:37,967
<i>- Gabo! What happened?!
- Papa!</i>

575
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:40,200
<i>- Papa! Papa!
- Code blue! Code blue!</i>

576
00:26:40,333 --> 00:26:43,667
<i>Your father really can't
rely on you.</i>

577
00:26:43,833 --> 00:26:45,833
<i>Doc, please do everything
to save my father!</i>

578
00:26:45,967 --> 00:26:46,933
<i> Pa!</i>

579
00:26:47,067 --> 00:26:49,000
- [FLATLINES]
<i> - Pa!</i>
